{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793641941,"nonce":"OmX1dgu84//iRC0ZBBl89jBDIdw=","title":"Interpreted frames take the global collector registry mutex twice","message":"hir_interp.rs boxes a FrameView per interpreted frame and registers it with collector::add_root_range_with, removing it on drop. With the built-in collector on (zypy, zylua) each is a lock of the global REGISTRY mutex plus a BTreeMap insert or remove. The same mutex guards large-block alloc and free and is held for a whole collection.\n\nEvery interpreter-served call pays this: first calls, stub-interpreted native calls, functions the interpreter refuses to compile. Adds to the first-iteration latency in deltablue, meteor, spectral.\n\nDirection: thread-local list of live frames that the collector walks; no lock or BTreeMap.","files":null}]}